there are too many families who came  here to give birth but left grieving the  death of their baby mistakes have been  made and repeated now the police will  investigate whether the trust or any of  its staff should face criminal charges  ready Isabella Stanton Davis should have  an older sister Richard and Rhiannon's  first daughter but Kate only lived for a  few hours this was the first and last  time Rhiannon was able to hold her we  didn't know what's going on I'd never  held a newborn baby before I seemed  everything was normal you know Kate  didn't want to feed or anything bad and  I never saw Kate alive again I was shown  Kate in a side room and told that the  situation was really poor and I cradled  Kate while she died in my arms just six  hours after hear Rihanna had given birth  to her so this is her but Kate should be  11 now in the years since her death her  family have written cards and wrapped  presents for every birthday and  Christmas they've also learned her death  could have been avoided if doctors and  midwives had recognized she was  seriously ill before it was too late  since Kate died her parents have fought  to uncover failings at the trust with  hundreds of cases now being investigated  they welcomed the involvement of the  police where one death is avoidable it's  avoidable that's that's criminal that is  criminal to have hundreds and hundreds  where the learning has not been taken  forward there's no question has never  been a question in my mind the assistant  Chief Constable of West Mercia Police  said we can confirm that a police  investigation will be conducted to  explore whether there is evidence to  support a criminal case either against  the trust or any individuals involved an  independent midwife led investigation is  already underway in April 2017 then  Health Secretary Jeremy Hunt announced  the investigation into a cluster of a  double baby deaths at the trust it  initially focused on 23 cases where  failings were alleged by A